# Every entry here has a written justification in the deploy repo's
# docs/CVE-TRIAGE.md (aaronmhmr/crypto-exchange-deploy) and an expiry -- this
# file is a deliberate, reviewed allow-list, not a way to make CI green.
# Re-run Trivy and re-evaluate at each expiry date.

# --- Django 4.1.13 (pinned deliberately -- see docs/CVE-TRIAGE.md) ---
# CVE-2025-64459: CRITICAL SQL injection. Real, unmitigated. Fixed only in
# 4.2.26/5.1.14/5.2.8. Accepted short-term because upgrading Django is
# app-level work, not "minimal changes to containerize" -- see the
# production-readiness roadmap in README.md. Expiry: 2026-10-15 (re-evaluate;
# do not let this sit past one month).
CVE-2025-64459
# CVE-2025-57833: HIGH SQLi in FilteredRelation. This app's ORM usage
# (grepped) never constructs a FilteredRelation with user-controlled column
# aliases -- not reachable in this codebase today, but still a real bug in
# the pinned Django. Expiry: 2026-10-15.
CVE-2025-57833
# CVE-2025-64458: HIGH DoS, Windows-only code path. This app only ever runs
# on Linux containers. Not reachable. Expiry: 2027-03-06 (long: genuinely
# inapplicable to this deployment target, not a "we'll fix it later" item).
CVE-2025-64458

# --- perl-base (Debian base image, not invoked by this app) ---
# CVE-2026-13221 (CRITICAL) and the perl-Archive-Tar/perl-IO-Compress/
# Storable findings below: perl ships as part of debian-slim's base layer;
# nothing in this image's CMD/entrypoint/dependency chain invokes perl.
# Fixed by rebuilding on a newer base image once Debian ships a patch.
# Expiry: 2026-10-15 (tied to the next scheduled base-image refresh).
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-9538

# --- util-linux family (bsdutils/libblkid1/liblastlog2-2/libmount1/
# libsmartcols1/libuuid1/login/mount/util-linux) ---
# All four CVEs require operations this container's process never performs
# (external mount helpers, nsenter --join-cgroup, X-mount options) and none
# are reachable from a non-root, no-new-privileges, single-process
# container with no privileged mount capability. No fixed version published
# by Debian yet as of this scan. Expiry: 2026-10-15.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# --- Other base-image OS packages, no fixed version yet / not reachable ---
# gzip: CVE-2026-41992 (LZH decompression -- this app never decompresses
# untrusted .lzh input).
CVE-2026-41992
# libacl1: CVE-2026-54369 (symlink traversal in ACL functions -- not called
# by this app or by Django/gunicorn).
CVE-2026-54369
# ncurses (libncursesw6/libtinfo6/ncurses-base/ncurses-bin): CVE-2025-69720,
# terminal-UI buffer overflow. No interactive TTY app runs in this
# container.
CVE-2025-69720
# libsqlite3-0: CVE-2026-11822/11824 (FTS5/heap overflow). This app's
# DATABASES uses PostgreSQL exclusively; sqlite3 is an unused transitive
# base-image dependency.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824
# systemd (libsystemd0/libudev1): CVE-2026-16742 is a systemd-homed
# privilege-escalation bug. systemd-homed does not run in this container
# (no init system, no systemd services active).
CVE-2026-16742

# --- Vendored frontend static assets (upstream Bootstrap admin template,
# not our code, not processed server-side) ---
# TinyMCE 6.1.0: CVE-2026-47759/47761/47762 (client-side XSS in the rich
# text editor widget). Fixing it means replacing a vendored third-party
# asset, out of scope for "minimal changes to containerize". Verified
# (grep across Exchange/) that dashboard/base.html and users/base.html
# load tinymce.min.js on every page, but tinymce.init() is never called
# anywhere in the codebase -- no editor instance is ever activated, so the
# specific vectors (data-mce-* attribute injection, mce:protected comment
# parsing) have no live editor surface to exploit. The script merely ships
# to the browser inert. Expiry: 2026-12-01 (revisit if TinyMCE is ever
# actually wired up to a textarea).
CVE-2026-47759
CVE-2026-47761
CVE-2026-47762

# --- Build-time-only Python packages ---
# wheel 0.45.1 (CVE-2026-24049) and jaraco.context 5.3.0 (CVE-2026-23949)
# are transitive pip/setuptools build tooling that ends up in the venv but
# is never imported or executed at runtime by this app or by gunicorn.
CVE-2026-24049
CVE-2026-23949
